  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Project Scope**\n\nOkay, I\'m now delving into the architectural instructions to flesh out the starter MCP project for Qlik Sense. The goal is clear: script comparison and summary reporting. I\'m focusing on parsing the provided prompt and instructions to understand the necessary components. I am exploring approaches to organize the structure of the starter project, and ensure the project incorporates clear script comparisons and summarization mechanisms.\n\n\n**Defining Architectural Layers**\n\nI am now focusing on the architectural layers specified, especially how they will translate to code structure within the Qlik Sense MCP project. The goal is to enforce the separation of concerns and ensure each layer fulfills its purpose. The instructions are clearly dictating a specific framework; the task is to ensure the project adheres to the specific constraints and requirements. I\'m prioritizing the creation of robust Server/SDK and Tools layers.\n\n\n**Mapping Project Framework**\n\nI am now structuring the Google AI SDK integration within the Qlik Sense MCP project. The Node.js runtime and ESModules layout is being implemented, based on the provided directory structure. I am ensuring that the Gemini-specific OpenAPI 3.0 JSON Schema spec (with explicit types) is correctly handled. I am implementing the core integration server, focusing on the specified 4-layer architecture, with clear delineation of Server, Tools, Handlers and Services layers.\n\n\n**Structuring Backend Components**\n\nI am now focusing on the backend components, specifically how to implement the integration server as an Express app. I\'m considering serving an API or webhook, but the instructions point to a `src/index.ts` entry point, so I\'ll prioritize that. I\'m examining the provided directory structure (`src/`, `server/`) and considering the Vite dev server setup with `tsx server.ts` as the entry point. I\'ll check `package.json` for script modifications and implement a script comparison and summarization function, as it is the core Qlik business logic.\n\n\n**Refining Entry Point and Structure**\n\nI am now structuring the backend and frontend components. I am prioritizing the Express server, given the specified `src/index.ts` entry point, which will be the heart of this project. But that would conflict with the typical Vite app layout, which defaults to `main.tsx` for the React app. I will place the Express backend in `src/`, with a minimal React UI to interact with it, because it is an AI Studio applet to be viewed in an iframe.\n\n\n**Implementing Backend Server**\n\nI\'m now structuring the project with a small UI to hit the backend route for script comparison and summary reporting. I\'ll prioritize a layout that will use an Express server in `server.ts` or `/src/index.ts`. I will update the `package.json` file with the relevant scripts, including a `build` script to package the backend for deployment. The UI will be minimally developed to ensure communication with the backend.\n\n\n**Integrating API Routes**\n\nI\'m now structuring the project to ensure `server.ts` handles both Vite middleware and the backend logic in `src/index.ts`. This seems optimal, as it serves both roles. I will begin by modifying `metadata.json` and `.env.example` according to the provided instructions. I will then create necessary backend files. It will be important to ensure the Gemini client/webhook is properly exposed in the main entry point, `src/index.ts`.\n\n\n**Constructing Directory Layout**\n\nI am now focusing on setting up the specified directory structure, particularly the backend components. I\'m prioritizing the creation of `server.ts` as the Express server, while ensuring `src/index.ts` serves as the export point for Gemini integration, and other required files, such as `src/server/gemini-client.ts` and `src/server/tool-registry.ts`. I will now start creating files, such as `src/tools/governance-tools.ts`, to house governance functionality.\n\n\n**Defining Tool Specifications**\n\nI\'m now adjusting the code to handle potential discrepancies with `@google/genai` imports. I will now adjust to accommodate possible variations in the `FunctionDeclaration` definition, either by importing the appropriate interface or by using an `any` type, or omitting the type altogether. I will now start focusing on the tools index to export all tools, such as the `compare_scripts` function, properly.\n\n\n**Finalizing Function Imports**\n\nI am now focusing on exporting the `allTools` array and ensuring the import paths are correct for the governance tools. I\'ve ensured `ExecutionContext` and `defaultContext` are exported, too, and made sure Qlik app service properly logs and uses a mock API client, to compare script functionality. The logic is now well-defined for tenant information and script comparison.\n\n\n**Implementing Mock API**\n\nI am now focusing on implementing the mock API calls to facilitate the script comparison functionality. I have integrated the `apiClient` mock into the service layer, replacing external calls. I am now updating logging and error handling, making sure that it adheres to specified conventions, and then preparing for testing and integration. I am also making sure that governance tools are correctly integrated.\n\n\n**Refining Handler Integration**\n\nI am now focusing on refining the handler integration within the `index.ts` file, ensuring seamless connections to the governance tools. I\'ve focused on `handleGetTenantInfo` and `handleCompareScripts`, to ensure they properly interact with the `qlikAppService`. The main task is to verify they can be called, so the logic is correct.\n\n\n**Connecting Handler Framework**\n\nI am now connecting the handler framework to the governance tools. I\'ve integrated `handleGetTenantInfo` and `handleCompareScripts` within the `handler-router.ts` file, and ensured they are correctly called via the `executeFunctionCall` function. I\'m focusing on error handling and proper logging for each function call to maintain system integrity.\n\n\n**Testing API Endpoint**\n\nI\'m now focusing on testing the API endpoint by calling `executeFunctionCall`. I\'ll verify the integration of the handler with governance tools, particularly within `src/index.ts`. I will now verify the correct execution of the functions from tools, ensuring they are properly invoked via the API.\n\n\n**Refining Express Server**\n\nI am now structuring the `server.ts` file to properly integrate with the Vite dev server. The focus is to ensure the Express server handles both API endpoints and the Vite middleware for serving the frontend. I am implementing the `/api/health` endpoint and `/api/gemini/chat` and incorporating logic to correctly call the MCP server, and integrate its Gemini client, to handle function calls.\n\n\n**Finalizing Gemini Integration**\n\nI am now focusing on the final integration with Gemini, and ensuring the `server.ts` file correctly handles responses from the Gemini API, especially within the `/api/gemini/chat` route. The handler now processes responses, and formats a final JSON object suitable for the endpoint, managing both text and function call responses. I have also implemented error handling to properly manage exceptions.\n\n\n**Constructing Minimal UI**\n\nI\'m now building the frontend UI, focusing on the script comparison feature. I\'ll create a minimal React app to interact with the backend API, allowing the user to input two Qlik app IDs. The plan is to trigger the comparison and summary generation on button click, fetching data from the backend. The Express server, which is currently running, is prepared for this interaction.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 33
      nanos: 579407855
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
